'''Silk Road''' (シルクロード, ''Shiruku Rōdo'', '''Silk Road''') is the 20th sub-chapter of [[Stories of Legend]]. It was added in [[Version 3.0 Update|Version 3.0]] and is available up to {{4c}} difficulty. In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], it is the 13th sub-chapter in the Stories of Legend and is available up to 3★ difficulty.

==Difficulty==
Silk Road is by far the hardest sub-chapter up to this point. Every stage here is at least somewhat challenging and requires a different strategy, so expect to change your lineup frequently. Having most (if not all) of the [[:Category:Crazed Cats|Crazed Cats]] and [[True Form]] [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]] is highly recommended for this sub-chapter.

One of the hardest stages is [[Marco Po Road]], which becomes almost unbeatable if the player doesn't win fast enough, and doing so isn't easy due to the presence of [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and the sheer amount of HP on the enemy base. However, it can be cheesed using [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Tank Cat]]. Another one of the hardest stages is [[Godiego Pass]], which contains three [[Dober P.D]]s. Unlike [[Pigpen Taboo]], however, the stage gives the player [[Shadow Boxer K|a source of money]] throughout the battle.
{{LegendDiff|140|160|140}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces three new enemies:
*[[Ginger Snache]]: A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemy with many knockbacks and good movement speed and attack damage. Often appears in large groups.
*[[Wall Doge]]: A defensive enemy with high health, low damage, slow movement speed and very short range. Can be considered an enemy counterpart of [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cat]].
*[[Sunfish Jones]]: An [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] enemy with massive health, exceptional range and the ability to slow down cats.
*While not his first appearance in-game, [[Super Metal Hippoe]] is introduced to Stories of Legend here. He has high health and knockbacks for a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy, moderate damage, fast movement speed and a guaranteed chance to knockback cats he hits.

