==Trivia==
*The name of this sub-chapter is a direct reference to the [[wikipedia:Silk Road|Silk Road]], which was a trade route primarily supplying spices across the East and Western landmass. It started from the second millennium BC and is now a railroad, as constructed in 2013 according to the Belt and Road initiative.
*[[Godiego Pass]] is named after the Japanese band [[wikipedia:Godiego|Godiego]], while [[Gandara's Rest]] and [[Monkey Magic]] are references to the songs "[[wikipedia:Gandhara (song)|Gandhara]]" and "[[wikipedia:Monkey Magic (song)|Monkey Magic]]" from Godiego's ''[[wikipedia:Magic Monkey|Magic Monkey]]'' LP. One of the lyrics to "Gandhara", "His very own utopia," is also referenced by [[Utopia is Over There]].
*Since they're all part of the same sub-chapter, the stages Monkey Magic, [[Outsider's Gate]], [[Pig Swill]] and [[Imp's cold sweat]] may be referencing the Chinese novel ''[[wikipedia:Journey to the West|Journey to the West]]''. Outsider's Gate's Japanese name is Foreign Land's Gate, which would represent the travelers crossing over to a [[wikipedia:Dvipa|dvipa]] in chapter 22, while the other three stages would be referencing Sun Wukong (a monkey), Zhu Bajie (a pig) and Sha Wujing (often depicted as a [[wikipedia:Kappa (folklore)|''kappa'']], which are mentioned in Imp's cold sweat's Japanese name).

